<title>ARGENTINA: ARGENTINE CASH SOYBEANS SURGE.</title>
<headline>ARGENTINE CASH SOYBEANS SURGE.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine soybean prices shot up in thin volume on the Buenos Aires Cereals Exchange Wednesday, in the wake of Chicago's gains on U.S. dry weather worries, dealers said.</p>
<p>Spot soybeans were up $5 a tonne and May soybeans rose $3, with scant offer helping the sharp gains. Sunseed prices were unchanged, weighed down by crushers' thin margins.</p>
<p>Maize spot and new crop advanced $1-2 and new wheat was unchanged, while spot firmed $1-2 a tonne on crusher demand.</p>
<p>((-- Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
